    ["June 1982 onward", f"Sustained equatorial westerlies west of the Date Line from June {c('harrison1984')}", f"Preceded by an anomalous southerly band at 150°–160°E crossing the equator from as far south as the Tasman Sea {c('harrison1984')}", f"These westerlies induced the initial strong equatorial warming east of the Date Line (author's interpretation) {c('harrison1984')}; a June–July downwelling Kelvin wave raised Christmas Island sea level about 25 cm in July, and it stayed high to December {c('rk2007')}; undercurrent at 159°W decayed in August {c('firing1983')}", "Proposed trigger of the vigorous phase; the June–July wave possibly set the timing and amplitude of the event (two studies)", "Preceded by MJO convection moving from the Indian Ocean (Roundy and Kiladis; our late-June window); July burst after it (RMM 0.65–1.07)", "B (event and ocean response); B (contribution, not isolated)"],
    ["Through November 1982", f"‘A succession of westerly pulses’ until November, citing Sadler (1983) and Harrison (1984) — indirect {c('chufrederick1990')}", "Not described in the sources read", f"Basin-wide adjustment, undercurrent reversal, sea-level and thermocline changes {c('firing1983', 'halpern1983')}", "Amplifier (general theory plus event observations)", "Late-Aug burst not supported as MJO; Nov bursts on the El Niño westerly background", "C (individual pulses not documented)"],
